        answer: "A partial exchange happens when an investor does not reinvest every dollar of net sale proceeds into replacement property. The reinvested portion still defers tax under Section 1031, while the remaining portion, called boot, is recognized as taxable gain in the year of the sale. The Qualified Intermediary manages both the reinvested funds and the boot distribution through the same exchange structure.",
